# os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local run artifacts: server logs, pid files, and anything an end-to-end check leaves behind.
# `.e2e-cookies.txt` holds a live session cookie — a credential, and never a thing to commit.
#
# Matched by PREFIX, not by suffix. The rules here were `.mermaid-*.log` and `.mermaid-*.pid`,
# which covered `.mermaid-3002.log` and `.mermaid-3002.err.log` but silently missed
# `.mermaid-3002.log.err` — so a server error log sat untracked-and-unignored, one `git add -A`
# from being committed. Error logs are exactly the file that captures a connection string or a
# patient name in a stack trace, so the pattern matches the whole family rather than the two
# suffixes someone thought of first.
.mermaid-*
.e2e-*

# Real-data audit output is PHI. `scripts/revenue-leak-audit.ts` refuses to write a real report
# anywhere inside this repository; this line is the second guard, for a report someone copies in by
# hand. (The synthetic demonstration lives in docs/pilot/synthetic-audit/ and IS committed.)
docs/pilot/audit-output/
*.phi.*

# Screenshot sweeps from scripts/shoot.mjs: PNGs and a measurement report, regenerated on
# demand and never a source of truth. Committing them would put ~4MB of binaries in every clone
# to record what one command reproduces in a minute.
.screens/
